.vite/

# Harness scratch buffer — crash-resilient agent working notes (.harness/ itself is
# committed; only the temp/ scratch dir is ignored, so records under
# .harness/records/ stay tracked).
.harness/temp/

# Installed skill copies are DERIVED artifacts of the published
# @ai-substrate/engineering-harness package, not source. They are produced by
# `harness skills install` (which shells `npx skills add`) and must never be
# committed — re-create them with the command in AGENTS.md:
#   - .harness/skills.lock.json — harness-owned per-project install lock (targets + scope)
#   - /skills-lock.json         — the vercel `skills` tool's own lockfile (written at cwd)
#   - .claude/skills/           — installed skill copies (project-local `-a claude-code`)
#   - .agents/                  — the canonical project-local skill store
.harness/skills.lock.json
/skills-lock.json
.claude/skills/
.agents/
